`LLMModel` gains a **Kind** (chat or embedding, defaulting to chat), and `services/llm.py` refuses a mismatch in both directions before any network traffic. The mistake this catches is rarely calling the wrong endpoint - it is configuring triage with an embedding model and reading a provider's error about token limits at three in the morning.

The Similar Tickets panel's default `max_distance` is **0.15**, measured rather than guessed. Against `nomic-embed-text` with real tickets, a genuinely related problem scores 0.09-0.10 and unrelated text - a broken coffee machine, against a corpus of network faults - scores 0.22-0.24. Short network tickets share vocabulary even when the problems are not related, so the useful band is far narrower than a general-purpose default suggests. `docs/admin/rag.md` says how to find the number for your own corpus and model.
